# PointMe Project Implementation Guidelines

## Architectural Enforcement
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Service Layer] --> B[React Components]
    C[Hooks] --> B
    D[API Routes] --> A
    E[Toast Service] --> B
    F[Auth Service] --> B
    G[Error Handling] --> H[Centralized Pattern]
```

## Code Validation Matrix
| Category        | Standard                  | Current Compliance |
|-----------------|---------------------------|-------------------|
| TypeScript      | Zero Any Types            | 92%               |
| Supabase        | SSR Package Only          | 100%              |
| Component Reuse | Existing Before New       | 85%               |
| Error Handling  | Centralized Pattern       | 78%               |
| Component Casing| PascalCase Consistency    | In Progress       |

## File Structure
```
src/
├── app/                # Next.js app router pages
├── components/         # UI components
│   ├── providers/      # Context providers
│   └── ui/             # Reusable UI components
├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks
│   ├── auth/           # Authentication hooks
│   ├── business/       # Business logic hooks
│   └── ui/             # UI-related hooks
├── lib/                # Core services and utilities
│   ├── core/           # Core functionality
│   │   ├── auth/       # Authentication services
│   │   └── toast/      # Toast notification service
│   └── supabase/       # Supabase client and services
└── types/              # TypeScript type definitions
```

## Coding Standards
- Use PascalCase for component names (e.g., TextArea not Textarea)
- Use camelCase for variables, functions, and file names
- Prefer functional components with hooks over class components
- Implement proper type definitions (avoid 'any' types)
- Use index files for clean exports
- Follow singleton pattern for service implementations

## Critical Services

### Toast Service
```typescript
// Correct usage
ToastService.success('Operation completed successfully');
ToastService.error('Something went wrong');

// Incorrect usage (deprecated)
ToastService.toast.success('Operation completed successfully');
```

### Auth Service
```typescript
// Correct usage
import { AuthService } from '@/lib/core/auth';

// For authentication operations
await AuthService.signIn(email, password);

// For error handling
try {
  await AuthService.signUp(email, password);
} catch (error) {
  // Use centralized error handling
  ErrorService.handleAuthError(error);
}
```

